{
  "schema_version": "0.2.0",
  "decision": "count_locally_for_fixedfloat_only",
  "rationale": "Every engine attaches a per-process request guard to a swap provider. It counts calls only on FixedFloat's own host (ff.io, or a subdomain of it), because FixedFloat allows 250 weight a minute per API key with a create costing 50 and blocks a key for longer each time it goes over. There the guard keeps the calls in a window within a 200 soft cap, and the calls that are not creates (status, refund, catalog) may use at most 50 of it between them, so open swap screens polling their status can never starve new swaps: at least three creates a minute always fit, four when nothing else ran. Every other host (Lightning Swap, a provider this library does not know, a test fake, a value that is not a URL) gets no local count at all: the provider limits its own accounts and says so with a 429, and a local count of this library's own could only refuse payers the provider would have accepted. On every host the guard obeys a 429: it stands off for the wait the provider names (Retry-After, or the wait in the response body), and for its profile's default when it names none.",
  "window_seconds": 60,
  "profiles_note": "`local_budget` is the per-window count the guard keeps, or null when it keeps none and only obeys the provider's 429. In it, `soft_cap` is the weight every call in one window may add up to, `non_create_cap` the part of it the calls that are not creates may use between them, and a create may bring the window up to the whole soft cap. `backoff_seconds` is the stand-off after a 429 that names no wait; a named wait is rounded up and kept between `min_backoff_seconds` and `max_backoff_seconds`. `create_backoff_only` is true when a 429 that answered a create stops creates only, so status and refund calls for swaps that already exist keep working; a 429 on any other path always stops every call.",
  "profiles": {
    "fixedfloat": {
      "local_budget": {
        "soft_cap": 200,
        "non_create_cap": 50,
        "create_weight": 50,
        "default_weight": 1
      },
      "backoff_seconds": 60,
      "min_backoff_seconds": 60,
      "max_backoff_seconds": 3600,
      "create_backoff_only": false
    },
    "provider-only": {
      "local_budget": null,
      "backoff_seconds": 60,
      "min_backoff_seconds": 1,
      "max_backoff_seconds": 300,
      "create_backoff_only": true
    }
  },
